course: dictionary
lesson: 15358
title: Somerset, a place name
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Somerset is a proper noun. It is the name of a particular place, so it starts with a capital letter. Somerset is a county in the south-west of England, which means a region of the country with its own name and borders.
explain: «We drove to Somerset to see the green hills and farms.» The word Somerset tells you where. You can find it on a map of England, in the south-west.
explain: Be careful: a «somersault» is a forward roll in the air. The two words look and sound similar, but they mean completely different things. Ask yourself: is it a place or a roll?
explain: «Dad bought a bottle of Somerset cider.» Cider is an apple drink, and Somerset is famous for it. The words around a name are clues, so look at them to work out what kind of word you are reading.
fact: Somerset is a county in the south-west of England.
fact: Somerset is famous for farms, apples, cider and Cheddar cheese.
fact: The city of Bath is in Somerset, and so are the towns of Glastonbury and Wells.
fact: The Somerset Levels are low, flat lands that flood in winter.
fact: Somerset is also used in place names in other countries, such as towns in Australia and the USA.
exercise: «We drove to Somerset to see the farms.» Where is Somerset? | A city in Scotland | A kind of forward roll | A type of cheese | *A county in the south-west of England
exercise: Which word means a forward roll in the air? | Levels | Cheddar | Somerset | *Somersault
exercise: «The Somerset Levels flood in winter.» Which is true of the Somerset Levels? | They are in Scotland | They are tall mountains covered in snow | *They are low, flat land that floods in winter | They are a type of apple
test: Which city is in Somerset? | London | Edinburgh | *Bath | Cardiff
test: Why does Somerset start with a capital letter? | *Because it is the name of a place | Because it always starts a sentence | Because it is a verb | Because it is a long word
exam: «Dad bought a bottle of Somerset cider at the market.» What does the word Somerset tell you about the cider? | It is a roll in the air | It was made in Scotland | *It comes from Somerset, a county in the south-west of England | It is a kind of cheese
